  "title": "Etiquettes of The Evening (Isha) Prayers",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "When the twilight sets, you may utter the azan and eqaamah statements for the Evening Prayer, observing all the aforesaid etiquettes. You may then perform the Evening Prayer, observing all of its etiquettes and meeting all of its conditions. It is highly advisable to prolong the Qunoot in this prayer and the post-prayer utterances, because there is enough time to do so. Accordingly, you may say all the supplications of mornings and evenings as well as all supplications dedicated to evenings, which are numerous. One of these is the sustenance-seeking supplication, which is mentioned in [Ta’qeebaat of Isha Prayers](D10). The supplication begins with these statements: اَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّهُ لَيْسَ لِيْ عِلْمٌ بِمَوْضِعِ رِزْقِيْ...\nIt is also recommended to recite [Surah al-Qadr](A101) six times and then say the following supplicatory prayer:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ رَبَّ السَّمٰوَاتِ السَّبْعِ وَ مَا اَظَلَّتْ وَ رَبَّ الْاَرَضِيْنَ السَّبْعِ وَ مَا اَقَلَّتْ وَ رَبَّ الشَّيَاطِيْنِ وَ مَا اَضَلَّتْ وَ رَبَّ الرِّيَاحِ وَ مَا ذَرَتْ اَللّٰهُمَّ رَبَّ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ وَ اِلٰهَ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ وَ مَلِيْكَ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ اَنْتَ اللّٰهُ الْمُقْتَدِرُ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ اَنْتَ اللّٰهُ الْاَوَّلُ فَلَا شَىْءَ قَبْلَكَ وَ اَنْتَ الْاٰخِرُ فَلَا شَىْءَ بَعْدَكَ وَ اَنْتَ الظَّاهِرُ فَلَا شَىْءَ فَوْقَكَ وَ اَنْتَ الْبَاطِنُ فَلَا شَىْءَ دُوْنَكَ رَبَّ جَبْرَاۤئِيْلَ وَمِيْكَاۤئيْلَ وَاِسْرَافِيْلَ وَاِلٰهَ اِبْرَاهِيْمَ وَ اِسْمَاعِيْلَ وَ اِسْحَاقَ وَ يَعْقُوْبَ وَ الْاَسْبَاطِ اَسْئَلُكَ اَنْ تُصَلِّىَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّ اٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ وَ اَنْ تَوَلَّانِىْ بِرَحْمَتِكَ وَ لَا تُسَلِّطَ عَلَىَّ اَحَدًا مِّنْ خَلْقِكَ مِمَّنْ لَا طَاقَةَ لِىْ بِهٖ اَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّىْ اَتَحَبَّبُ اِلَيْكَ فَحَبِّبْنِىْ وَ فِى النَّاسِ فَعَزِّزْنِىْ وَ مِنْ شَرِّ الشَّيَاطِيْنِ الْجِنِّ وَ الْاِنْسِ فَسَلِّمْنِىْ يَا رَبَّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ وَ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّ اٰلِهٖ.\nALLAAHUMMA RABBAS SAMAAWAATIS SAB-E’ WA MAA AZALLAT WA RABBAL ARAZEENAS SAB-E’ WA MAA AQALLAT WA RABBA SHAYAATEENE WA MAA AZALLAT WA RABBAR REYAAHE WA MAA ZARAT ALLAAHUMMA RABBA KULLE SHAY-IN WA ELAAHA KULLE SHAY-IN WA MALEEKA KULLE SHAY-IN ANTAL LAAHUL MUQTADERO A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN ANTAL LAAHUL AWWALO FALAA SHAY-A QABLAKA WA ANTAL AAKHERO FALAA SHAY-A BA’-DAKA WA ANTAZ ZAAHERO FALAA SHAY-A FAWQAKA WA ANTAL BAATENO FALAA SHAY-A DOONAKA RABBA JABRAA-EELA WA MEEKAA-EELA WA ISRAAFEELA WA ELAAHA IBRAAHEEMA WA ISMAA-E’ELA WA ISHAAQA WA YA’-QOOBA WAL ASBAATE AS-ALOKA AN TOSALLEYA A’LAA MOHAMMADINW WA AALE MOHAMMADIN WA AN TAWALLAANEE BERAHMATEKA WA LAA TOSALLETA A’LAYYA AHADAM MIN KHALQEKA MIMMAN LAA TAAQATA LEE BEHI ALLAAHUMMA INNEE ATAHABBABO ELAYKA FA-HABBIBNEE WA FIN-NAASE FA-A’ZZIZNEE WA MIN SHARRISH SHAYAATEENIL JINNE WAL INSE FA-SALLIMNEE YAA RABBAL A’ALAMEENA WA SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADINW WA AALEHI.\nO Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and what they overshadow, and Lord of the seven earths and what they carry, and Lord of the devils and those they lead astray, and Lord of the winds and what they scatter. O Allah, Lord of everything, God of everything, and Sovereign of everything; You are Allah, the All-Powerful over all things. You are Allah, the First, so there is nothing before You; and You are the Last, so there is nothing after You; and You are the Manifest, so there is nothing above You; and You are the Hidden, so there is nothing beyond You. Lord of Gabriel, Michael, and Raphael; and God of Abraham, Ishmael, Isaac, Jacob, and the Tribes. I ask You to bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, to take charge of me with Your mercy, and not to give power over me to anyone from Your creation whom I have no strength to withstand. O Allah, I seek Your love, so make me beloved [to You]; and grant me honor among the people; and from the evil of the devils among jinn and mankind, keep me safe, O Lord of the Worlds. And bless Muhammad and his family.\nYou may then pray Almighty Allah for any thing you wish.\nYou may thereafter do the thanksgiving prostration after which you may offer the Wutayrah Prayer, which is a supererogatory (mustahab / naafelah) prayer that is offered in the sitting position after the Evening Prayer and consisting of two units of prayer in both of which it is recommended to recite one hundred verses of the Holy Qur’an. It is therefore preferable to recite [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) and [Surah al-Waqiah](A60) (No. 56) in the first unit and [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) in the second.\nUpon accomplishment, you may say any supplication you wish to say."
